/-!
# Checked Scoped HE Worker Adequacy

This module proves closed-annotation adequacy and local correspondence laws for
the checked configuration-scoped HE worker. The downstream
`FirstSuccessScopedRecursiveAdequacy` module uses these laws to earn its
ordinary recursive profile. The local controls below alone do not establish
that principal theorem or its remaining construct extensions.

1. **Closed-Annotation Transfer (`ClosedTypeAnnotations`)**:
   Whenever a space has closed type declarations (`∀ subject, ∀ sig ∈ getAtomTypes space subject,
   atomVariables sig = []`), `invocationTypes state = rawTypeLookup state.space` holds at every
   configuration `state`. Consequently, `Checked.machine dispatch scopedTypes` and
   `Checked.machine dispatch rawTypes` have identical `next`, `blocked`, `step`, and `run`
   semantics, lifting all 10 `Covered` recursive derivation families (`AtomDerivation`,
   `TupleDerivation`, `ArgsDerivation`, `CallDerivation`, `ReturnDerivation`,
   `ProducedDerivation`, `RawInvocationDerivation`, `MinimalDerivation`,
   `PrimitiveDerivation`, `FunctionBodyDerivation`) directly to `scopedTypes` without
   duplicating the derivation tree, while preserving `ReadoutCertificate` and
   `BindingTheoryEquivAt` at every emitted result.

2. **Concrete Schematic Polymorphic Invocation & Paired Sibling Controls (`ScopedPolymorphicCompletion`)**:
   Completes the concrete `ScopedPolymorphicInvocation` run from its head-cast checkpoint (`afterHead`)
   to `.finished` (52 steps), and proves the concrete 141-step paired polymorphic sibling control
   `(Pair (ident $x) (ident true))` under `(: ident (-> $t $t))` and `(= (ident $y) $y)`
   with open caller aliases (`$caller ↦ $x`, `$t ↦ Number`).

3. **Contextual Machine Specializations, Restricted Joint Witness & Same-Space Renaming Bridge (`ContextualAndRenamingBridge`)**:
   Specializes the contextual adequacy theorems (`contextual_scoped_source_iff_finished`,
   `contextual_scoped_atom_iff_steps`) to `Completed.scopedLookup`, constructs the restricted
   empty-public-scope joint witness `nestedPriority_scoped_worker_contextual_aligned`, and proves
   same-space renaming transport (`steps_rename_scopedLookup_same_space`, `scopedTypeLookup_rename_space_iff`).

4. **Concrete Positive and Negative Controls (Controls A–E, `ScopedWorkerControls`)**:
   Kernel-checked controls for repeated polymorphic sibling calls with open caller aliases,
   polymorphic correlation rejection, duplicate equation multiplicity, pause/grant residual
   alignment, and the cyclic raw match admission boundary.

5. **Universal Local Scoped Cast & Head-Cast Squares (`UniversalScopedCastAndHeadBoundary`)**:
   Proves `scopedLookup_of_invocationTypes_related`, the enabling bridge
   `scoped_worker_symbol_cast_enabling_bridge`, the fresh-symbol cast local square
   `scoped_fresh_symbol_cast_local_square`, and the repeated-arrow head-cast local square
   `scoped_fresh_arrow_head_cast_local_square` under arbitrary retained `state.stack` and `state.emitted`.

6. **Structural Retained Configuration & Local Transition Correspondence (`ScopedRetainedRelation`)**:
   Defines `ScopedActivationRel`, `ScopedResultRel`, `ScopedAtomEntryReady`, `ScopedTaskRel`,
   `ScopedFrameRel`, `ScopedControlRel`, and `ScopedConfigurationRel` with explicit non-supported
   host/snapshot/context exclusions, proves depth-grant invariance (`ScopedConfigurationRel.deepen`,
   `ScopedConfigurationRel.replenish`, `ScopedConfigurationRel.atom_zero_suspends_and_grants`),
   proves the negative reentry discriminator (`ScopedAtomEntryReady.held_reuse_not_ready_and_delivers`),
   and establishes commuting local continuation, diagnostic/fallback/filter, and recursive task
   and expression-entry squares (`publish_step`, `finish_step`, `append_step`, `prepend_step`,
   `prependDiagnostics_empty_step`, `prependDiagnostics_noErrors_step`, `fallback_nonempty_step`,
   `fallback_exhausted_step`, `filter_publish_step`, `singleton_step`, `tupleTail_step`,
   `functionTail_step`, `argumentTail_step`, `calls_step`, `heads_step`, `headsContinue_step`,
   `argumentHeads_step`, `argumentHeadsContinue_step`, `tupleHeads_step`,
   `invocationReturnOrdinary_step`, `minimalResults_step`, `chainResults_step`, `bodyResults_step`,
   `tupleNil_step`, `tupleSingleton_task_step`, `tupleCons_step`, `branchesNil_step`,
   `argumentsNil_step`, `argumentBranchesNil_step`, `functionBranchesNil_step`,
   `invocationsNil_step`, `invocationsCons_step`, `callsNil_step`, `callsCons_step`,
   `returnsNil_step`, `productionsNil_step`, `minimalsNil_step`, `chainRowsNil_step`,
   `bodyResultsNil_step`, `returnRefused_step`, `returnEvaluate_step`, `atomEmptyOrError_step`,
   `atomTypePass_step`, `func_functionStart_step`, `argsSingleton_step`, `bodyStart_step`,
   `scoped_nonfunction_expression_fallback_square`, `scoped_undefined_operator_tuple_square`,
   `scoped_empty_types_selection_failed_square`, `invocationScanRel_of_select_and_applicationChecks`).

7. **Activation-Preserving Cast & Polymorphic Function-Entry Configuration Squares (`UniversalScopedPolymorphicApplication`)**:
   Lifts fresh-symbol and repeated-arrow presentation matching through `Entry.Value.UnifyRel.lift`
   to construct `Completed.Frame` witnesses satisfying `ScopedActivationRel`, proving the
   configuration-level cast squares `scoped_fresh_symbol_cast_configuration_square` and
   `scoped_fresh_arrow_head_cast_configuration_square`, the earned polymorphic unary-arrow
   application entry square `scoped_polymorphic_function_entry_configuration_square`, and the
   executed retained caller-alias control `controlF_polymorphic_function_entry_with_caller_alias`.
-/

